I need to prove:
- ClientA: `F.Large((s + t) + u, k)` given `F.Size(s) > k`
- ClientB: `F.Large(s + (t + u), k)` given `F.Size(t) > k`

For ClientA:
1. Use `ConcatA(s, t)` to get `Size(s + t) == Size(s) + Size(t)`, so `Size(s + t) > k`
2. Use `ConcatA(s + t, u)` to get `Size((s + t) + u) == Size(s + t) + Size(u)`, so `Size((s + t) + u) > k`
3. Use `Finish((s + t) + u, k)` to get `Large((s + t) + u, k)`

For ClientB:
1. Use `ConcatA(t, u)` to get `Size(t + u) == Size(t) + Size(u)`, so `Size(t + u) > k`
2. Use `ConcatA(s, t + u)` to get `Size(s + (t + u)) == Size(s) + Size(t + u)`, so `Size(s + (t + u)) > k`
3. Use `Finish(s + (t + u), k)` to get `Large(s + (t + u), k)`

{"ClientA.dfy":"include "Facts.dfy"
module ClientA {
  import F = Facts`ViewA
  lemma Prove(s: seq<int>, t: seq<int>, u: seq<int>, k: nat)
    requires F.Size(s) > k
    ensures F.Large((s + t) + u, k)
  {
    F.ConcatA(s, t);
    F.ConcatA(s + t, u);
    F.Finish((s + t) + u, k);
  }
}
","ClientB.dfy":"include "Facts.dfy"
module ClientB {
  import F = Facts`ViewA
  lemma Prove(s: seq<int>, t: seq<int>, u: seq<int>, k: nat)
    requires F.Size(t) > k
    ensures F.Large(s + (t + u), k)
  {
    F.ConcatA(t, u);
    F.ConcatA(s, t + u);
    F.Finish(s + (t + u), k);
  }
}
"}

